# Implementation Bias

## Default Response Style
When working in this repo:
- be concise
- give the recommendation first
- prefer file edits and code scaffolding over long explanations
- make assumptions explicit
- call out risks directly

## Required Output Pattern
Use this structure when relevant:

### Recommendation
State the clearest answer first.

### Why
Brief rationale.

### Risks / Tradeoffs
Main limitations or risks.

### Decision Needed
What requires user input.

### Next Actions
Immediate concrete next steps.

## Push Back On
- overbuilding the sync layer before historical migration works
- assuming all data maps cleanly
- skipping validation and reconciliation
- adding UI before backend workflows are proven
- vague pilot ownership models